rec('pacl-land-cis-refunds','PACL: unregistered land-linked schemes, agent payments and investor recovery','SEBI found PACL’s land-linked plans to be unregistered collective investment schemes in August 2014. The source records ₹43.6478 billion of collections during 26 February 2013–15 June 2014, a separate historical commission route, and associate land-holding arrangements. Court-directed recovery subsequently produced ₹3,720.67 crore of cumulative refunds against 35,74,401 eligible applications by 5 May 2026; property objections and auction work continued in September 2026.',PO+PB+PC+PR+['pacl-refund-extension','pacl-reuters-2015'],P,'2014-08-22',['pacl-ltd','pacl-investors','pacl-agents','pacl-sellers','pacl-associates','sebi','supreme-court','lodha-committee','pacl-assets'],['pacl-collections','pacl-agent-commissions','pacl-seller-payments','pacl-associate-land','sebi-pacl-order','sc-lodha-mandate','lodha-asset-administration','lodha-refunds','lodha-bengaluru-tender'],'2013–2014 collections and 2014 regulatory finding; recovery observations through September 2026','PACL argued that it sold/developed land and relied on judicially verified deeds. SEBI rejected the CIS defence but expressly preserved genuinely certified sale deeds. SAT upheld the order in 2015. The September 2026 Supreme Court order disposes of specific property objections, not the whole case; bank-deficient refund applications had a rectification window through 6 October 2026.',kind='investigation-case',status='Regulatory finding with ongoing court-directed recovery; no criminal-conviction claim',asof='2026-09-30',end='2026-09-30',amounts=[newcollections,refund],limits=['Historical mobilisation, current liability, auction value, bank balance and refunds are different quantities; no net-loss estimate or recovery percentage derived.','This is a bounded public-source case, not a complete ledger of PACL entities, investors or criminal proceedings.'],alts=['Some certified land transactions were genuine and are expressly protected by the 2014 order.','Bank-account deficiencies and property-title objections can delay payments without themselves proving fresh diversion.'],falsifier='Reconcile scheme bank ledgers, paid commission schedules, genuine registered deeds, auction sale receipts and application-level refund acknowledgements without exposing investors’ private account data; later reasoned orders may change property eligibility or recovery status.')
rec('pacl-response-and-genuine-deeds','PACL response: land-sale defence and genuine-deed protection','PACL claimed a real-estate business, invoked Justice K. Swamidurai’s verification of 19,284 sale deeds and proposed a five-year repayment arrangement. SEBI rejected the broader CIS defence, citing the 500-customer sample with no completed sale deed, while paragraph 37 expressly protects sale deeds certified as genuine.',PO,P,'2014-08-22',['pacl-ltd','sebi','pacl-investors'],['pacl-collections','pacl-agent-commissions','pacl-seller-payments','pacl-associate-land','sebi-pacl-order'],'2014 submissions and order','The order cannot be paraphrased as finding every land sale fictitious. Historical certified deeds are counter-evidence to that overbroad claim; they did not defeat the scheme-level CIS finding.',kind='respondent-response',limits=['The 500-customer sample finding does not mean no customer ever received land. No outcome of a distinct criminal prosecution is asserted.'])
rec('pacl-money-stages','PACL amounts: in-window collections versus historical mobilisation and commissions','SEBI records exact collections of ₹43,647,808,345 during 26 February 2013–15 June 2014. Its approximately ₹49,100 crore historical mobilisation combines a through-March-2012 aggregate with that period while expressly missing April 2012–25 February 2013. PACL-reported ₹7,893.80 crore paid commissions through March 2012 differ from prepaid-commission accounting figures.',PO,P,'2014-08-22',['pacl-ltd','pacl-investors','pacl-agents'],['pacl-collections','pacl-agent-commissions'],'Amounts carry different historical periods; the evidence event is the August 2014 order','PACL explained commissions as payments to agents under its land plans. SEBI questioned the advance-commission structure. The amounts cannot be summed as separate investor losses.',kind='financial-stage-control',amounts=[newcollections,historic,commission],limits=['No audited net-loss or current unpaid principal is supplied by these aggregates. Historical commissions partly predate the atlas window.'])
rec('pacl-current-recovery','PACL recovery status: paid refunds, auction values and unresolved eligibility','The May 2026 observation reports ₹3,720.67 crore cumulative refunds, approximately ₹3,894 crore of property auction value and approximately ₹1,200 crore in the designated bank account. The August notice confirms some applications could not be processed because of bank-verification deficiencies. On 9 September the Supreme Court accepted specified objection recommendations, sought verification for others and listed the matter for 8 October 2026.',PB+PC+['pacl-refund-extension'],P,'2026-05-05',['lodha-committee','pacl-investors','pacl-assets','supreme-court','sebi'],['lodha-asset-administration','lodha-refunds','sc-lodha-mandate'],'Financial observation as of 5 May 2026; procedural updates 3 August and 9 September 2026','The board’s reference to eligible claims must be read with the subsequent deficient-application notice. Neither ₹3,894 crore auction value nor ₹1,200 crore bank balance is another refund payment. The court’s acceptance of particular property objections limits any blanket assertion that restrained assets all belong to PACL.',kind='outcome-record',asof='2026-09-09',end='2026-09-09',amounts=[refund,auction,bank],limits=['No later cumulative refund figure or independently reconciled auction-cash figure established. Scheduled 8 October hearing is not treated as completed.'])
rec('pacl-bengaluru-auction','Bengaluru Rural: named recovery-sale administrators, no completed sale yet','The 30 September 2026 tender identifies StockHolding Document Management Services Limited as auction-assistance agency and C1 India Private Limited as e-auction service provider. It expressly says the Lodha Committee is not the property owner. November 2026 bid/auction dates are prospective.',PR,P,'2026-09-30',['lodha-committee','stockholding-dms','c1-india','bengaluru-auction'],['lodha-stockholding','c1-auction-platform','lodha-bengaluru-tender'],'Tender issuance 30 September 2026; future auction schedule','These companies are named only for recovery administration. The source establishes no wrongdoing, auction purchase, fee amount or receipt by either provider.',kind='recovery-process',states=['KA'],limits=['Bengaluru Rural location is explicitly sourced; no parcel centroid or map coordinate invented.'])
rec('chapwa-toll-debarment','Chapwa toll collection: disputed ₹50 transaction and debarment set aside','NHAI alleged an unrecorded ₹50 cash collection and false exemption entry during a Chapwa inspection, imposed a ₹10 lakh penalty and later terminated/debarred Ganeshgarhia. The ₹6.821 crore annual remittance was the contractor’s obligation to NHAI. On 11 December 2025 the Delhi High Court set aside only the debarment for failure to consider the defence and give reasons; it reserved factual conclusions and left contractual remedies for termination and penalty.',CH,T,'2024-07-25',['nhai','ganeshgarhia','chapwa-contract','ihmcl','delhi-hc'],['nhai-chapwa-contract','ganeshgarhia-remittance','ihmcl-inspection-referral','nhai-chapwa-allegation','nhai-chapwa-penalty','nhai-chapwa-debarment','dhc-chapwa-relief'],'Contract July 2024; inspection February 2025; enforcement June 2025; judgment December 2025','Ganeshgarhia denied unauthorised software use and disputed the fraud inference, pointing to local-resident treatment and the correctly recorded return journey. NHAI said the inspection vehicle was not local and a valid exemption pass was necessary. Court relief addresses the defective decision process; no final factual finding or later penalty recovery is established.',kind='investigation-case',tier='alleged',status='Disputed contractual allegation; one-year debarment set aside 11 December 2025',asof='2025-12-11',end='2025-12-11',amounts=[annual,cash,penalty],states=['UP'],limits=['Later status search through 7 October 2026 did not establish an appeal or separate contractual outcome. This is last verified judicial status, not a guarantee that nothing else occurred.','This is a specific Chapwa case; do not merge it into March 2025 nationwide debarments or September 2026 ED searches without source evidence.'],alts=['The contractor described a local-resident exchange/exemption rather than systematic diversion.','The authority relied on different ingress and egress accounting and its interpretation of the contractual requirements.'],falsifier='Compare timestamped official ETC records, camera evidence, exemption eligibility, receipts and contractor remittance ledgers; require a reasoned order addressing the contractor’s actual reply before upgrading disputed facts.')
rec('chapwa-company-response','Ganeshgarhia response: disputed software allegation and unaddressed defence','The contractor denied unauthorised software use, said no device had been seized and complained that particulars and supporting materials were not supplied. It relied on its local-resident/exemption explanation and the ₹70 return trip recorded by NHAI’s system, and argued the ₹10 lakh penalty had not been implemented.',CH,T,'2025-05-15',['ganeshgarhia','nhai','delhi-hc'],['nhai-chapwa-allegation','nhai-chapwa-penalty','nhai-chapwa-debarment'],'15 May 2025 reply and submissions recorded in 11 December 2025 judgment','NHAI disputed the local exemption, characterised the vehicle as its deployed inspection vehicle, and maintained that accounting irregularity justified action. The court required these points to be addressed, without resolving the underlying factual dispute.',kind='respondent-response',asof='2025-12-11',end='2025-12-11',states=['UP'],limits=['A defence recorded by a court is not necessarily a finding accepting its truth.'])
rec('chapwa-court-outcome','Delhi High Court outcome: debarment set aside, contractual claims left open','Paragraphs 30–40 hold the debarment order unreasoned and procedurally deficient; paragraph 36 notes no POS machine/system/device was seized. Paragraph 34 expressly refrains from factual conclusions. Paragraph 41 declines interference with contract termination and penalty because contractual/civil remedies must be used.',CH,T,'2025-12-11',['delhi-hc','ganeshgarhia','nhai'],['dhc-chapwa-relief','nhai-chapwa-debarment','nhai-chapwa-penalty'],'Judgment pronounced 11 December 2025','The result is neither a continuing one-year ban nor a merits finding that no irregularity occurred. Non-interference with penalty is not proof of its recovery or a judgment affirming all NHAI factual allegations.',kind='outcome-record',states=['UP'],limits=['The judgment’s concluding paragraph contains a contract-year discrepancy; original 25 July 2024 contract date is identified from paragraphs 1–2 and reproduced work order.'])
rec('chapwa-money-stages','Chapwa amounts: remittance obligation, disputed collection and assessed penalty','₹6,82,10,000 is the annual contractual remittance from Ganeshgarhia to NHAI, ₹50 is the disputed single inspection collection and ₹10,00,000 is an imposed penalty with actual recovery unverified. They are not additive diversion amounts.',CH,T,'2025-12-11',['ganeshgarhia','nhai','chapwa-contract'],['ganeshgarhia-remittance','nhai-chapwa-allegation','nhai-chapwa-penalty'],'Separate contract, inspection and penalty stages','The contractor said the penalty was not implemented; the High Court left penalty/termination to contractual remedies. No bank evidence establishes paid annual remittances, penalty encashment or total loss.',kind='financial-stage-control',amounts=[annual,cash,penalty],states=['UP'],limits=['Do not portray a ₹6.821 crore NHAI payment to the contractor or calculate a ₹25 loss by applying the 50% clause to an unresolved fact pattern.'])

